==Enemy==
The Relic variant of [[One Horn]], Oldhorn is extremely resilient, with 2.4 million health and 30,000 DPS when unbuffed. He slowly approaches the [[Cat Base]] at 4 movement speed.

==Strategy==
When you first encounter this time-traveling terror, he's the only thing in the entire stage, making it easy to build an entire set dedicated to defeating him. Otherwise, things might complicate if other enemies get in the way.

[[Freshman Cat Jobs (Super Rare Cat)|Prof. Cat Jobs]] makes this enemy very easy by reducing his damage down to a mere 120 per hit. With the help of "Weaken" Effect UP [[Cat Combo|Combos]], he'll barely even push. [[Onmyoji Cat (Rare Cat)|Thaumaturge Cat]] can do the same, but only weakens to 50%. Oldhorn's short range leaves him highly vulnerable to crowd-control, so you can slow/freeze/knock him back with cats like [[Boogie Cat (Special Cat)|Gato Amigo]], [[Li'l Nyandam (Special Cat)|Dark Emperor Catdam]], [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Cat]], [[Medusa Cat (Rare Cat)|Twintail Medusa Cat]], [[Delinquent Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Ultra Delinquent Cat]] and [[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Cat Mask Doron]]. A [[Talents|Talented]] [[Cat Gunslinger (Rare Cat)|Rodeo Cat]] and [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Mystic Uril]] can likewise prove themselves useful for keeping him at bay, as they can keep him almost permanently slowed. When his advance has stopped, you can then use attackers like [[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:N2]] or [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] to take huge chunks out of his health pool.

