==Trivia==
*His Japanese name, Koraino-kun, is a pun on 古来 ''korai'' (from ancient times) and ライノ ''raino'' (rhino).
*In the Korean version, Oldhorn is named like a variant of [[Bore]]. Oldhorn is 고대 보어 ''Godae Bo-eo'' ("Ancient Bore") while Bore is 샤이 보어 ''Syai Bo-eo'' ("Shy Bore").
*He has the shortest range of all [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relics]].
*Despite being introduced before [[Sir Rel]], Oldhorn is listed after him in the [[Enemy Guide]] and has a higher ID.

